format session-log-v1
stamp 20260815.030651
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host cloud pier (Eastern EDT convention)
title ALES130 — Lotus's stereo_fade: the fade envelope carried into stereo, one shared ramp, both channels in lockstep
prompt Continue the recurring baton (prin recur) on the ALES/Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think Fifth lap of this recur run. ALES129 opened the stereo amplitude class on its crux (normalize, one measured shared scalar). This rung carries the class's most-reached-for member, ALES4's fade — the click-free fade-in and fade-out. A fade differs from normalize in a clarifying way: its gain is a positional RAMP the caller names, not a measured scalar, so the stereo lift is validation-first (like the span edits), not measurement-first — and because a positional gain is identical for both channels, the SAME ramp preserves the image for free.
think Read fade.rye: fade(clip, start, count, num0, num1, den), FadeError = {BadGain (zero den), BadRange (span outside)}. Matched the shared-validation pattern from stereo_silence_span: assert balance, check den==0 then span once against the shared length before either channel mutates, then run mono fade per channel with the SAME ramp. Reused fade.FadeError by name.
think Wrote design read, module, witness. Four laws: stereo fade law (each channel == ALES4's fade with the same ramp byte for byte, fade-in and fade-out), balance/length law (equal-length, both hold starting length), shared-ramp image law (a 1:2 master keeps its 1:2 ratio at every seat, an identical-channel master stays identical), atomicity/degenerate law (BadRange and BadGain each leave both channels untouched and balanced, count=0 the identity, sub-span fade leaving the rest untouched). One red caught and fixed: my peak-lowering flourish used a fade-out, whose first sample stays at full gain, so the peak held — LeftPeakNotLowered. Changed it to a half→zero ramp that attenuates every seat, so the peak strictly drops. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean.
obs The amplitude class now has its measured-scalar member (normalize) and its positional-ramp member (fade) side by side, and the contrast is the lesson: normalize shares ONE measured number across channels to hold the image, fade shares the WHOLE ramp — different mechanisms, same image-preserving end. The self-caught peak red is a small reds-first win: a wrong assumption about fade-out geometry, caught by the witness on metal before the send. No custody gate reached — purely local software, self-approved design round.
loom witness=ales_stereo_fade_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 reds_caught=1
file lotus/stereo_fade.rye ALES130 — stereo_fade, the fade envelope lifted to stereo: one shared ramp on both channels, validated once, four laws with the shared-ramp image crux.
file tools/ales_stereo_fade_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-fade line.
file active-designing/20260815-030651_fill-ales130-lotus-stereo-fade.md the self-approved design read for this rung.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES130 roster entry and stamp.
recommend keep-going the stereo amplitude class is climbing; the next mechanical laps lift the remaining value/amplitude ops (halve, rectify) to stereo, each trivial per-channel where the image is unaffected — no gate reached.
